wed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5fce90c8bcc2ff0ba9ba59178074558d0c21b1d271d616b49c38ccf2761e8f7f","compact":"5096585489bf206de51ee73b3a53ef103725dffeb368fae5a51ff6362c87d766","nasal":"5096585489bf206de51ee73b3a53ef103725dffeb368fae5a51ff6362c87d766"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":7,"english":"What my mother-in-law instructed me at the time that I was leaving for the lonely and fearful forest, is constantly present in my mind.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0618e263fb7e738bd5c8a812b685205d299242ba2be11a073ccad9453a142bdd","compact":"99ca4142c29337f53f7d7ea96c29a2a774d3e691eb7303c4a264640eb1d23274","nasal":"e131f70a1d4e3876ab00dd7035d80c077f1e3323ad54a11ace90ca42e459e832"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":8,"english":"And what also my mother taught me in presence of fire on the occasion of the bestowal of my hand, is also remembered by me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.682,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a3fc0f9e0144208169a0e666fa14c49fd2d8815920a8e259805479577fc5159c","compact":"1587ca5201460d0420f419280dbe2c870c7f62b3fa3d042c966aa43d0f7de85a","nasal":"1587ca5201460d0420f419280dbe2c870c7f62b3fa3d042c966aa43d0f7de85a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":9,"english":"And, O you engaged in acts of righteousness, I have not forgotten the words that my relatives said to me, viz, the asceticism of a woman is ministering to her husband. They did not teach any thing else.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.551,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"213c7eefd5fd38d4be464ee4955eedfeff170006a28def43b6312a0327c14d81","compact":"5e158ba81768ecbb66aa03dd2eb259f042c696d3e4b3fc3de2fcea2f9c8dde55","nasal":"6f283e26fe81881cb6ae88918ca2c486ff609c872f06ce181dc7d8da3e724cea"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":10,"english":"Having served her lord. Sāvitri is highly honoured in heaven; and you also, following the same course, by virtue of having served your husband, has secured heaven.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34c6c65c3d4bbd10f155e548673bc0099f1609200e8efbb08e9c7688436df71f","compact":"4c50a0d87ce13fe4d97be501bf2fe80e6d5a07457cad00dd6cbe1372e52fdeec","nasal":"4c50a0d87ce13fe4d97be501bf2fe80e6d5a07457cad00dd6cbe1372e52fdeec"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":11,"english":"And this foremost of females, this goddess of heaven, Rohiņi, is not seen for a moment without the moon.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b8106375d6d1f5c932bbf61cd43fb4d87c999fbc8ee01130193a7422f411c510","compact":"64fda35477988ba2567c07f13138ea6c4de33301abcc696666faa117c7abc4ad","nasal":"9428073762e9dc0494a6c4c52cc39e2ccde94579bf4f6db7ac0e06b74a67ec31"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":12,"english":"And prime women of this sort, firm in their husbands, are highly respected in the celestial regions by virtue of their pious acts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0540079514827b3987645ec3e511682572fec6e6383fd9d66f7056224bb18347","compact":"3d1a03f7c4af9cff59cdc9350d657f492129e492694f51e0e563cb239dd4ed39","nasal":"4a29c017171a82936dc4781862606622d781db8ec7b425922761bf897ae5a986"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":13,"english":"Hearing Sītā's words, Anasuyā, exceedingly delighted, smelling her head, spoke thus, pleasing Maithili.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.738,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1fab9713fcb59fac8865d6a8eb4ffcfd2e2bf824a0c69d05f9f793557fa7576d","compact":"1410132f3be363300b20fd4481f6423ec61e8cbad528f27bb0fa8957e7943f8a","nasal":"024b3bf253c6ba90bfa9a8cfd6a809094fab774f34f5b52cb7561f8baff8efdb"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":14,"english":"By observing restrictions, I have earned great asceticism. By resorting to that energy, I would, O Sīta, confer a boon upon you, O you of pure vows.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e364f4a89062c61b01ac3cdb5423c9d3acf652ee588b5a2a1ab1f46d1846e1ac","compact":"d16b1710d7c05b42c7de634909e1bcf1092f17662bd0423123553e236ba90742","nasal":"13d6