s), was struck with amazement.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.768,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110028","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fef19223afabd2682efa82128b4b6ad342245c3e2902a0adbf7efdfc7d23a3c6","compact":"f894b3bea26ef85fd080f2697aef7f6ab7f57bc2fad1d35437cbfa718ef990c4","nasal":"9197ea53dd7bc54c78b343f0fac7593f2514c09efd6d06d2764e6c5f22ae1c47"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-29","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":29,"english":"Being childless, he took me on his lap from affection, and saying, 'This is my daughter', conceived affection for me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110029","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf03c121004c3d243fec4db6c3ee66103a99e9a07752567c0ac23d08e6f7882f","compact":"cd5a27b6e912ff6cb0ecc913ebbb72d751b88f99c3312e7df589a2c5e292f367","nasal":"952ccfc0865d368faeb8f5373bb89f76e986f998d875781ce5d99c606b1fe415"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-30","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":30,"english":"Then there were uttered words in the welkin, resembling those of a human being,! 'O king, in all righteousness, this is your daughter'.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.846,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110030","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d2cbd398766653ee46c7f14b483ded8579cd256f856dac76609d5a11ce6451cb","compact":"ff37e2113a49f761c9f5d98265e3ed4f3df7376971e2365e26920c566ea535c2","nasal":"b3f68ffe3cafca34bdb335577beb76be74443f890801b1574987574409a5d110"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-31","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":31,"english":"Then well-pleased, my righteous father, the king, lord of Mithilā, receiving me, attained mighty good fortune.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110031","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4039c39e41c6300890ddacd0c2872bae121c7551a943bf7bc14c51d48fe2cf86","compact":"c7604502bd7534d5d68eb3df1d41807651043948b0a2132fd3ab47a6a14fc9ca","nasal":"c7604502bd7534d5d68eb3df1d41807651043948b0a2132fd3ab47a6a14fc9ca"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-32","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":32,"english":"Consigned to the pious eldest noble one (queen), desirous of having offspring, I was brought up by that mild lady, with the tenderness of a mother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.753,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110032","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ec80861d83da33b62d27f1c6602a0bff8860f640b11b4278c241ca7d9f4534c","compact":"0d677d3cbc860ae829a4893a438db5e3e5b816351a004babd7b11aa5693c4d96","nasal":"0d677d3cbc860ae829a4893a438db5e3e5b816351a004babd7b11aa5693c4d96"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-33","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":33,"english":"(In time) seeing me fit for the company of a husband, my father in distress was plunged in thought, like a poor man that has lost his wealth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110033","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fee13b52c7bbd827223a465095cf38da93bd52e718c21ac79c8d54d2a8dada49","compact":"a25aeb0f4c06e92106b5502a31ac0beac1e303d7d9115f60ca0f1a1ecb6e9123","nasal":"db1221af552d0f8312fabb5a03b8c8af0f3995fe8ba05ed32c9f20ca10e36e4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-34","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":34,"english":"Even if the father of a girl be like to ſakra himself on earth he reaps odium at the hands of his equals and inferiors.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110034","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"05796fd563faf88f16df9b9949c6004ecde823f7a16779e573ca7c8f85685be2","compact":"f58327d3cc4aa3715e69d9beba7fb476b244979c78e93dfc22e02d2c1099dd7e","nasal":"f58327d3cc4aa3715e69d9beba7fb476b244979c78e93dfc22e02d2c1099dd7e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-35","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":35,"english":"Perceiving this obloquy at a short distance, the king was plunged in a sea of anxiety, but could not cross it, like one that has no raft.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110035","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3340e554df98f2d67d6d114ad78b6d7cc3dd060bbd35caf8eae753d508626288","compact":"e110167baebea2fcf40705475fec3cb4998443077a4c22202132f82acaff5a64","nasal":"3abc8a711940404299fe795c3d9411659c68c19eef8f7ed6b4b7c910a170e6f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-110-36","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":110,"verse":36,"english":"Knowing me as unborn from any female vessel, the lord of earth reflecting upon it, could not come upon a suitable and fit husband for me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-118-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2110036","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6365275114529e6f7b1ef7a97a42cac498424da14a27f1f64fc790d